  "finding": "The model resolves 25% of questions correctly against 88% for keyword matching, so on this vocabulary it is NOT worth its latency - a dozen lines of keyword matching does the same job instantly and deterministically. Refusal is the more important column: the model refuses correctly 0% of the time on questions this vocabulary cannot serve, versus 75% for the rules. The architectural point stands regardless of which wins: because resolution is constrained to a closed vocabulary, the worst failure available to either is picking the wrong governed metric, which is visible and reversible. Neither can invent a definition."
